Look for R2LCE (general VNswitch command reference) and R2LDE (general 
VNswitch technical overview). Here is a good start: 
http://ftp.uniroma2.it/Digital/compaq/archives/networks/

They don't contain explicit references to the CG, but it should be enough to 
get you started.

The output shows that the "easystart" loop has finished, hence no need to 
"stop" DRS. You're in "config only" mode. If you were confronted with the 
"*" prompt, the "talk 6" command would get you to the CONFIG process (or at 
least it does on things that run DRS).

So, just set the switches up (the general VNswith manuals and HELP are 
useful), then, give it a try.

I might have some of the other manuals, but I'd have to go looking through 
some archive stuff and that could take a while. It's probably best to 
contact me privately if you really need them.

-- 
Cheers, Colin.
