If that's all you'r trying to achieve, won't "automatic VNbus connection" on 
the DEChub 900 backplane, plus just layer 2 switching (the default) in the 
modules, plus setting an IP address in each module plus the backplane do 
what you need? OK, you might need to rattle through the "Config" process in 
each VNswitch to get them started in the first place, but I'd expect just 
giving them an IP address for normal and "host services only (for down-line 
loading firmware)" mode to be enough. You may find that just giving them an 
IP address and restarting them through the DEChub 900 console port redirect 
to the appropriate slot is enough.

ClearVisn V3.1 is necessary if you want to set up fast ethernet channels on 
the backplane and connect module ports to the backplane channels. The VNbus 
is an exception to that if you have automatic VNbus connection enabled in 
the DEChub 900.

You probably also want to make sure you have the latest firmware in the 
backplane and the modules. V5.6-1 for the hub, V3.4 for the VNswitches.

You might find a simple DECrepeater 90TS useful to act as the backplane 
agent for downloading firmware before you set up the VNswitches.

-- 
Cheers, Colin.
Legacy = Stuff that works properly! 




